 390: ## 2026-11-14 — Persistent Fixed 3D Viewport, Visible Sequential Cascade, and Global Cursor Parallax
 391: 
 392: ### Objective
 393: Resolve user issue where 3D cards disappeared upon scrolling down into "THE ARCHETYPES OF SANSKARAN" ("where are the cards ?"). Ensure cards remain prominently visible, cascade down one-by-one as user scrolls down, rise back up one-by-one on scroll up, and track the mouse cursor across the entire screen.
 394: 
 395: ### Root Cause Analysis
 396: 1. **Container Scrolled Out of View**: The WebGL container `<div ref={mountRef}>` was styled with `absolute inset-0` inside the `<section id="hero">`. When the user scrolled past the hero section, the entire container scrolled off-screen.
 397: 2. **Excessive Vertical Drop Formula**: `cascadeDropY` was set to `dropEased * 10.5`. In Three.js units with camera at $Z \approx 7.8$, a drop of 10.5 plunged the cards completely below the camera's bottom frustum boundary ($Y \approx -3.2$).
 398: 3. **Local Mouse Tracking Scope**: Pointer move listener was attached to `#hero`, preventing cursor updates once scrolled into other sections.
 399: 4. **Opaque Scene Background & Atmospheric Overlay**: Three.js had solid black `scene.background = new THREE.Color("#120E15")` and an 88% dark bottom gradient blocking visibility.
 400: 
 401: ### Changes Made
 402: - **Fixed Persistent Canvas**: Changed `<div ref={mountRef}>` to `fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none z-[1] overflow-hidden` so the 3D scene stays pinned to the viewport across all sections.
 403: - **Transparent WebGL Layer**: Removed `scene.background`, added `renderer.setClearColor(0x000000, 0)`, and enabled `alpha: true` so the global multi-layer `ParallaxBackground` shines through.
 404: - **Tuned Sequential Cascade**:
 405:   - `cardCascadeStagger = (i / CARD_COUNT) * 0.45`
 406:   - `rawDrop = THREE.MathUtils.clamp((scroll - cardCascadeStagger) * 1.8, 0, 1)`
 407:   - `cascadeDropY = dropEased * 1.9` (keeps cards comfortably in view on screen)
